Every computer's window shows and edits the whole fleet: a client changes the server's layout, options, hotkeys and settings, and the server or any client changes any other client's own settings (the server relays them), with each change applied at once and seen everywhere. Running cores restart by themselves when a change needs it, instead of waiting for "Apply and restart"; "Restart all" restarts every computer's core. Editing needs the computers to trust each other's certificates; the server asks to trust a computer of its layout when that computer's window connects.
